<title>USA: Georgia-Pacific to post $80 mln Q2 gain.</title>
<headline>Georgia-Pacific to post $80 mln Q2 gain.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georgia-Pacific West Inc said it will post an after-tax gain of about $80 million in the second quarter of 1997 on the sale of its Martell, California-based operations to Sierra Pacific Holding Co for about $320 million.</p>
<p>Georgia-Pacific said its expects the sale to close in the same quarter.  </p>
<p>Georgia-Pacific bought the 127,000-acre operation in 1988, although did not disclose the purchase price. The site, about 50 miles southeast of Sacramento, California, produces Western soft lumber and includes a particleboard operation.</p>
</text>
